<title>USA: ValuJet mechanics, inspectors OK union.</title>
<headline>ValuJet mechanics, inspectors OK union.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mechanics at ValuJet Inc have voted to join the Teamsters Union, the union said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Forty-two of the 70 mechanics and inspectors of the Atlanta-based airline voted for the union on Wednesday, and the results were released in mid-afternoon.</p>
<p>The union must now engage in negotiations with ValuJet management to put together a contract.</p>
<p>ValuJet returned to the skies on Monday for the first time since it was grounded after its Flight 592 crashed in the Florida Everglades in May, killing all 110 people on board.</p>
</text>
